From a0709aa65a4c45edbbbd349a0b99a588c6ae06f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:58:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] avfilter: Add V4L2 M2M format conversion, detiling and
 scaling filter

Stateless video decoders often produce a tiled layout that neither the
display controller nor the GPU can consume directly. MediaTek MT8195
decodes to MM21, which its display cannot scan out at all, but its MDP3
mem2mem device converts MM21 to linear NV12, UYVY or ARGB and can rescale
in the same pass.

Add a filter that hands DRM PRIME frames to such a device and returns DRM
PRIME frames in the requested format and size.

The V4L2 pixel format is what carries the tiling, so the input format is
matched on the DRM fourcc together with the format modifier rather than
the fourcc alone, which is what distinguishes MM21 from SUNXI_TILED_NV12
and from plain NV12. That is only known once a frame arrives, so the
mem2mem device is probed on first use rather than when the link is
configured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
